    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1354">

                <pb facs="1610" n="1412" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1412"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/7–2045: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1354<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-20T12:00:00+01:00">July 20, 1945—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7304. Embassy understands Foreign Office position unchanged by French proposals
                    (re Paris 525, July 18 to London<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1354-f1"/>) British still
                    unwilling proceed prior conclusion Big Three Meeting. Should meeting end in
                    time, and result in concurrence Soviet request as is expected, British will make
                    counter-proposal Tangier Conference to open August 6 instead August 3.</p>
                <p>Sent Dept as 7304; repeated Paris 467, Madrid
                    192, Tangier 45.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Winant</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
